# Team: We can fix him / Are we the bad guys? — Game Design Document

## 1. High-Level Game Pillars
> Rule: if a feature doesn’t reinforce a pillar, it’s cut or reworked.

Game Pillars
- Floor-level stealth and survival
- Risk–reward verticality (towers)
- Throw-based combat
- Human vs Alien power tension
- Relationship-driven recovery (healing events)

---

## 2. Core Gameplay Loop (One Pass Only)
Keep this short and readable.

Core Loop
1. Crawl through hostile area
2. Choose stealth or chaos
3. Defeat / bypass enemies with thrown items
4. Collect drops (money & ingredients)
5. Spend resources on upgrades
6. Recover and make relationship choices
7. Repeat with higher risk

Everything else plugs into this.

---

## 3. Player Systems (What the Player Can Do)

### 3.1 Movement System
States
- Crawling (default)
- Climbing (towers)

Design Rule  
The floor is safe. Height is power. Power costs risk.

Crawling
- Low visibility to enemies
- Can throw items
- Quiet movement
- Safe positioning

Climbing
- More visible
- Cannot throw items
- Can be knocked off
- Falling causes damage + alert

### 3.2 Verticality & Towers
Purpose
- Provide stealth positioning
- High-risk, high-reward encounters

Tower Interactions
- Enemies may:
  - Spot player more easily
  - Knock player off
  - Be pushed or dropped for instant kills
- Player gains:
  - Better stealth angles
  - Bonus drops for tower takedowns

### 3.3 Combat & Throwing
- Core combat method
- Supports:
  - Silent takedowns
  - Loud combat engagement
- First strike bonuses when enemy is Unaware

